.TH SCS-CRTREQUEST 1 "September 2026" "sslcrtsrv 0.8.4" "SSLCrtSrv Manual"
.SH NAME
scs-crtrequest \- request and renew certificates via acme.sh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scs-crtrequest
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scs-crtrequest
drives
.BR acme.sh (1)
to request and renew every approved-and-due certificate in one pass, or one
named certificate. It has no subcommands \(em behavior is selected entirely
by flags. Typically run unattended (e.g. from cron), with no
.B \-\-cert\-name
given so every approved certificate is processed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " PATH
Server config file to read the certificate directory and default ACME
provider from. Default
.IR /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json .
.TP
.BI "\-\-cert\-name " FQDNS
Act on one specific FQDNs set instead of every approved one.
.TP
.B \-\-staging
Request from the certificate authority's staging/test environment instead of
production.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Allow a staging certificate to overwrite an existing valid production one.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-acme
Add
.BR acme.sh 's
own
.B \-\-debug
flag to every invocation.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-check\-dns
By default, DNS delegation is checked before every issuance/renewal attempt,
and a certificate whose delegation isn't in place is skipped with a warning
instead of letting
.B acme.sh
fail on it. This flag disables that check entirely, restoring the
unconditional old behavior.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-dns\-only
Pure diagnostic: check DNS delegation and report, never call
.B acme.sh
or touch the database. Requires
.BR dig (1).
.TP
.B \-\-force\-dns\-refresh
Force a real re-issuance to push a freshly rotated DNS-provider token into
.BR acme.sh 's
saved state immediately. Consumes a real issuance per domain touched \(em not
for routine use.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
If this run finishes with one or more failures, also send an admin
notification via
.IR server_config.json 's
.B notifiers
/
.B notification_routing
(the
.B error
event) \(em a single message summarizing every error logged during the run.
Off by default; meant for unattended runs where nobody is watching stdout or
the log file.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json
\(em default configuration file.
.br
.I crtrequest.log
\(em typical redirected-output log path for a cron invocation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scs-server (1),
.BR scs-crtmanager (1),
.BR scs-admintui (1),
.BR scs-acme-server (1),
.BR acme.sh (1),
.BR dig (1)
.PP
The project's
.I Manual.MD
has the full narrative reference.
